  "worked_solution": "The coefficient of ${x}^{3}$ is $\\frac{1}{3!}{f}^{(3)}(0).$ Let's compute the necessary derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\frac{1}{1-x} \\\\ {f}^{\u2032}(x) & =\\frac{1}{(1-x)^{2}} \\\\ {f}^{\u2033}(x) & =\\frac{2}{(1-x)^{3}} \\\\ {f}^{\u2034}(x) & =\\frac{6}{(1-x)^{4}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate ${f}^{\u2034}(0),$ which gives\n\n$$\n{f}^{\u2034}(0)=\\frac{6}{(1-0)^{4}}=6.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{3!}{f}^{\u2034}(0)=\\frac{1}{6}\\cdot 6=1.\n$$\n\nSo the coefficient of ${x}^{3}$ is $1.$",
